WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.237
Module 13 combined statistics and visualization to help us describe and communicate data more clearly.

00:00:09.237 --> 00:00:14.727
You used mean, median, standard deviation, quartiles, and grouped summaries.

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:20.592
You created histograms, boxplots, bar charts, scatter plots, and line charts.

00:00:20.592 --> 00:00:28.823
You also introduced correlation and the idea of uncertainty through a simple confidence interval.

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:36.430
The most important lesson is that numbers and visuals should support the same analytical question.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:40.970
In Module 14, we will take one more step.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:48.315
We will introduce machine learning by connecting simple algebra to learned relationships, features, numeric vectors,

00:00:48.315 --> 00:00:51.540
train and test data, prediction, and evaluation.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:01:00.637
That final module is designed as a bridge into the machine learning course you will take next semester.
